se `keyboardActivation=\"manual\"` when focus should move independently of selection."},"1506":{"id":"/docs/components/tabs-31","page_id":"/docs/components/tabs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tabs#accessibility","content":"`overflowLabels` is optional and defaults to \"Previous tabs\" and \"Next tabs\". Provide localized labels when needed; they should describe the logical direction rather than physical directions like \"left\" or \"right\", as the component automatically handles RTL layouts."},"1507":{"id":"/docs/components/tabs-32","page_id":"/docs/components/tabs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tabs#accessibility","content":"`TabList` must be rendered inside `Tabs` and must provide `aria-label` or `aria-labelledby`. Give each `Tab` and its corresponding `TabPanel` the same `id`; React Aria uses that key to build their accessible relationship."},"1508":{"id":"/docs/components/tabs-33","page_id":"/docs/components/tabs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tabs#customization","content":"The component exposes state through data attributes:"},"1509":{"id":"/docs/components/tabs-34","page_id":"/docs/components/tabs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tabs#customization","content":"`Tabs`: `data-design=\"underline\"` or `data-design=\"manilla\"`."},"1510":{"id":"/docs/components/tabs-35","page_id":"/docs/components/tabs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tabs#customization","content":"`Tab`: `data-selected`, `data-hovered`, `data-pressed`, `data-focus-visible`, and `data-disabled`."},"1511":{"id":"/docs/components/tabs-36","page_id":"/docs/components/tabs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tabs#customization","content":"`TabPanel`: `data-inert` when a force-mounted inactive panel is not interactive."},"1512":{"id":"/docs/components/tabs-37","page_id":"/docs/components/tabs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tabs#customization","content":"Use these attributes to extend styling without replacing the accessibility behavior supplied by React Aria Components. You can also use render props in `className` to style based on state (e.g., `className={({ isSelected }) => isSelected ? 'active' : ''}`)."},"1513":{"id":"/docs/components/tabs-38","page_id":"/docs/components/tabs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tabs#customization","content":"Use `TabList`'s `containerProps` to customize the outer tab list shell, such as increasing its width."},"1514":{"id":"/docs/components/tabs-39","page_id":"/docs/components/tabs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tabs#best-practices","content":"Use Tabs for peer panels on the same page and URL."},"1515":{"id":"/docs/components/tabs-40","page_id":"/docs/components/tabs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tabs#best-practices","content":"Keep the number of tabs small enough for users to understand the available sections."},"1516":{"id":"/docs/components/tabs-41","page_id":"/docs/components/tabs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tabs#best-practices","content":"Do not use Tabs for primary application navigation or route changes."},"1517":{"id":"/docs/components/tabs-42","page_id":"/docs/components/tabs","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tabs#best-practices","content":"Do not render a standalone `Tab`; compose it inside `Tabs` and `TabList`."},"1518":{"id":"/docs/components/tag","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","type":"page","content":"Tag","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Components"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/tag"},"1519":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-0","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/components/tag","content":"Non-interactive labels that highlight statuses and categories."},"1520":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-1","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/components/tag#installation","content":"Installation"},"1521":{"id":"/docs/components/tag-2","page_id":"/docs/components/tag","