s` maps individual category values to palette color indices, overriding\nthe series color for just those bars — so a single series can carry a different color\nper category. All three periods here share the same category-to-color map, so each\nchannel keeps one color across every period; the comparison periods are dropped to\nreduced opacity."],[285,"`CheckboxGroup` is composed: write `Label`, a `Group` holding the `Checkbox` items, `Text slot=\"description\"`, and `FieldError`. The `Group` takes its axis, gap, and presentational role from the group's `orientation`, so a bare `<Group>` is all you need; pass your own `direction`/`gap` to lay the items out differently. Each `Checkbox` takes label text next to the indicator."],[355,"`ChipButton` for menu filters and other actions with a Chip-like appearance"],[373,"`ChipButton` is a real button and exposes menu state through `MenuTrigger`; provide an accessible name when the visible content is incomplete."],[351,"`ChipGroup` + `ChipList` + `Chip` for grouped values, selection, keyboard navigation, and removal"],[366,"`ChipGroup` owns selection and removal behavior. Use a Chip render prop for\nstate-dependent content, and `Button` with `slot=\"remove\"` together with\n`onRemove` for removable items. See **Toggle Chips** and **Removable Chips**."],[1777,"`className` and `style` apply to the tooltip panel."],[484,"`Collapsible`: `data-expanded`, `data-disabled`, and `data-focus-visible-within`."],[494,"`CollapsiblePanel` is labeled by its trigger through `aria-labelledby` automatically."],[495,"`CollapsiblePanel` uses `role=\"group\"` by default. Keep it when the panel's content does not need\na navigation landmark; there is no need to set it explicitly."],[486,"`CollapsiblePanel`: `data-focus-visible-within`."],[1997,"`colorIndex` pins each series to a palette color. Any series can use any index,\nindependently — here two pairs each share an index so an actual line and its\ndashed forecast read as the same color, distinguished only by line style."],[1114,"`currentStep` is the single source of truth for the timeline. Omit it for a not-yet-started flow where every step is `future`; pass the step count for a fully completed flow where every step is `past`."],[698,"`data-color`: Applied when color prop is set"],[701,"`data-flip`: Applied when flip prop is set (\"horizontal\" or \"vertical\")"],[697,"`data-icon`: The icon name (always present)"],[699,"`data-loading`: Applied during icon loading from CDN"],[700,"`data-mode`: Applied when mode prop is set (e.g., \"sprite\")"],[702,"`data-rotate`: Applied when rotate prop is set (90, 180, or 270)"],[1437,"`data-selected`, `data-hovered`, `data-pressed`, `data-focused`, `data-focus-visible`, `data-disabled`, `data-readonly`, `data-invalid`, `data-required`, `data-size`"],[434,"`DatePicker` (single) and `DateRangePicker` (range): a read-only formatted date label; the whole field opens a calendar popover"],[1587,"`Detail` is supporting copy, such as captions and metadata, on the detail ramp. It keeps the\nsurrounding color; add `emphasis=\"passive\"` to mute it."],[525,"`DrawerTrigger` wraps a trigger button and a `<Drawer>`, handling open\nstate automatically."],[619,"`emphasis` picks a feedback color and changes only the color."],[1578,"`emphasis` picks a feedback color and changes only the color."],[1586,"`emphasis` selects a feedback color and changes nothing else. Without it, text inherits the\nsurrounding color."],[1024,"`Enter/Space`"],[60,"`Enter` / `Space`"],[491,"`Enter` / `Space`"],[567,"`Enter` / `Space`"],[792,"`Enter` / `Space`"],[534,"`Escape`"],[950,"`Escape`"],[1026,"`Escape`"],[1782,"`Escape`"],[604,"`FileTrigger` adds no visuals or ARIA of its own — accessibility comes from the pressable child you provide. Use a component with an accessible name (e.g. an Antares `Button` with clear label text) so assistive technology announces the action. The underlying `<input>` is visually hidden but remains operable by keyboard through the child's press behavior."],[2066,"`Flex` is a one-dimensional layout component for arranging children in rows or columns with alignment and spacing control. It extends `Box`, inheriting all `Box` capabilities (padding, elevation, rounding, self-alignment, and polymorphic `as` prop)."],[706,"`focusable=\"false\"`: Prevents keyboard focus"],[2104,"`Grid` is a two-dimensional CSS Grid layout component for complex grid-based layouts. It extends `Box`, inheriting all `Box` capabilities (padding, elevation, rounding, self-alignment, and polymorphic `as` prop)."],[621,"`Heading` renders a semantic `h1`-`h6` element via the `level` prop.\nInside a `Modal`/`Dialog`, add `slot=\"title\"` and it labels the dialog automatically."],[498,"`Icon slot=\"indicator\"` is decorative and receives `aria-hidden=\"true\"` automatically."],[780,"`InlineDrawerPanel` is the collapsible content for the accordion pattern — a thin wrapper over RAC `DisclosurePanel` that hides when collapsed. The trigger is any component you slot in with `slot=\"trigger\"` — there's no dedicated trigger component."],[809,"`Input` is the single-line control inside a field, not a field on its own. Prefer `TextField` or `NumberField` as the parent; see those components for fuller examples."],[1980,"`legendPosition` puts the legend above or below the plot, or hides it with `null`. Multi-series charts get a bottom legend by default."],[622,"`level` sets the semantics and `size` sets the look, so the two never have to match. Without\n`size`, a heading takes the size scope's heading tier at any level."],[2035,"`lg` - Large spacing"],[839,"`ListBox` requires either `aria-label` or `aria-labelledby`. For a labeled, popover-style picker, prefer `Select`."],[2034,"`md` - Medium spacing"],[874,"`MenuTrigger` exposes its open state via `isOpen`/`onOpenChange`,\nwhich can be used to drive the rotation of a chevron icon."],[203,"`minValue` / `maxValue` bounds and `isDateUnavailable` per-day disabling"],[437,"`minValue` / `ma